  "contract": [
    "Reject bytes through the first finite NUL are read completely before source bytes, even when source is empty.",
    "Every reached payload position is read once per scan phase with an ordered volatile unsigned BYTE load. Duplicates in reject retain their input reads; only nonzero reject bytes set bitmap bits.",
    "Source NUL stops before membership or its own pointer advance. Every nonzero source byte advances the genuine cursor before membership, including a terminal hit that may leave one-past without dereference.",
    "Return the exact unsigned32 count of preceding nonzero nonmembers; terminal NUL/reject member is excluded. No signed cap, pointer subtraction, final reread or unused later-source-NUL requirement.",
    "Reached bytes are genuine live stable determinate readable raw storage, with nonwrapping 32-bit advances within/one-past the corresponding actual allocation. Interior, unaligned, read-only, identical and stable overlapping regions and ordinary caller-owned stack storage are admitted.",
    "No null or zero-count shortcut, padding, typed wide/input DWORD allocation, locale/Unicode/codepage interpretation, validation, SDK search/copy, provider, fallback, globals/TLS or caller binding.",
    "Native callee bitmap/frame/argument-home/saved-register self-alias protocols, faults, MMIO, mutation/concurrency and lifetime changes are excluded. No fake scratch-identity or argument-block parameter is introduced."
  ],
